vector: at 1, index 1, front 1, pop_back 1, insert 1, erase 1; in its bounds 0
array: at 1, index 1, a literal of too many 1
deque: at 1, back 1, pop_front 1, erase 1
list: a place that is none 1, an erased element's 1, the end's 1, next of the end 1, pop_front 1, splice of itself 1
forward_list: an erased element's place 1, erase_after the last 1, front 1
stack: top 1, pop 1; queue: front 1, pop 1; priority_queue: top 1, pop 1
set: the end's key 1, a place after an insert 1, after clear 1, after swap 1, erase_at of one 1
set: a place after inserts of elements that are there and erases of ones that are not 0
multiset: a place after an insert of an equal element 1
map: at of no key 1, a place after a new key 1, next of the end 1; a multimap's place after a second value of its key 1
map: a place after writes to keys that are there and erases of keys that are not 0
unordered_set: the end's key 1, a place after an insert 1, erase_at of one 1
unordered_set: a place after a reserve that makes a new table 1, after one that makes none 1, after rehash 1
unordered_set: a place after inserts of elements that are there and erases of ones that are not 0
unordered_map: at of no key 1, a place after a new key 1, next of the end 1; an unordered_multimap's place after a second value of its key 1
unordered_map: a place after writes to keys that are there and erases of keys that are not 0
